I'm saying they are not {cifnu}.


>   The definition of baby in English
>

We are talking about Lojban, not English


> is:
>
> : a very young child
>
> : a very young animal
>

sounds like {verba}

>
>   (source m-w.com)
>
>   All these case qualify.  I don't believe cifnu is that much different.
>

Please, read the definition once again.


> Words in brackets in the gismu list are rarely probative, and they
> explanatory or expanding, rather than limiting, the definition.
>

Then {verba}/{cifnu} distinction becomes moot.


> (Or are you suggesting that "flira" means the same as "stedu" because it
> says "head" in brackets?
>

Those brackets clarify which meaning of "face" is meant.


